1
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,402
( THUNDEROUS INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

2
00:02:19,080 --> 00:02:20,411
( SOFT INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

3
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:23,248
" JONATHAN : " The Diary of Jonathan Harker .

4
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:26,686
" Third Of May , 1885 . "

5
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:30,929
" At last my long journey is drawing to its close . "

6
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:34,605
" What the eventual end will be , I cannot foresee . "

7
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:37,724
" But whatever may happen , I can rest secure "

8
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:41,407
" that I will have done all in my power to achieve success . "

9
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:45,283
" The last lap of my journey from the village of Klausenburg "

10
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:48,648
" proved to be more difficult than I had anticipated "

11
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:52,611
" due to the reluctance on the part of the coach driver to take me all the way . "

12
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:55,001
" However , as there was no other transport available , "

13
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:58,243
" I was forced to travel the last few kilometers on foot "

14
00:02:58,320 --> 00:03:00,527
" before arriving at Castle Dracula . "

15
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:04,646
" The castle appeared innocuous enough in the warm afternoon sun , "

16
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:09,328
" and all seemed normal but for one thing . There were no birds singing . "

17
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:14,404
" As I crossed the wooden bridge and entered the gateway , "

18
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:17,560
" it suddenly seemed to become much colder "

19
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:22,528
" due , no doubt , to the icy waters of the mountain torrent I had just crossed . "

20
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:26,161
" However , I deemed myself lucky to have secured this post "

21
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:29,884
" and did not intend to falter in my purpose . "

22
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:46,924
( DOOR CREAKS OPEN )

23
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,644
( DOOR CREAKS SHUT )

24
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:25,607
( SOFT , EERIE INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

25
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:41,730
( CLOCK TICKING )

26
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:09,927
( SINISTER INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

27
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:28,725
I 'm sorry . I didn 't hear you come in .

28
00:06:34,200 --> 00:06:38,046
My name 's Jonathan Harker . I 'm the new librarian .

29
00:06:39,040 --> 00:06:41,202
You will help me , won 't you ?

30
00:06:43,200 --> 00:06:45,328
Say you will , please !

31
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:49,044
- How can I help you ? - Get me away from here .

32
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:52,364
- But why ? - He is keeping me prisoner .

33
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:56,005
Who is ? Count Dracula ?

34
00:06:57,840 --> 00:06:59,365
I 'm afraid I don 't understand .

35
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:03,964
Oh , please . Please help me to escape !

36
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:22,128
( OMINOUS INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

37
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:35,162
Mr Harker , I am glad that you have arrived safely .

38
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:36,927
Count Dracula ?

39
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:40,211
I am Dracula . And I welcome you to my house .

40
00:07:40,280 --> 00:07:43,045
I must apologise for not being here to greet you personally

41
00:07:43,120 --> 00:07:45,000
but I trust you 've found everything you needed .

42
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:47,720
Thank you , sir . It was most thoughtful .

43
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:50,128
It was the least I could do after such a journey .

44
00:07:50,200 --> 00:07:51,850
Yes , it is a long journey .

45
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:54,890
And tiring for you , no doubt . Permit me to show you to your room .

46
00:07:54,960 --> 00:07:56,166
Thank you , sir .

47
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:11,371
DRACULA : No , please , allow me .

48
00:08:13,200 --> 00:08:15,646
Unfortunately , my housekeeper is away at the moment .

49
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:18,451
- A family bereavement . You understand ? - Yes , of course .

50
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:19,616
DRACULA : However , I think you will find

51
00:08:19,640 --> 00:08:21,640
that everything has been prepared for your comfort .

52
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:23,016
JONATHAN : How soon may I start work , sir ?

53
00:08:23,040 --> 00:08:26,200
DRACULA : As soon as you wish . There are a large number of volumes to be indexed .

54
00:08:46,640 --> 00:08:48,529
Is there anything else you require , Mr Harker ?

55
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:51,046
No , I don 't think so . You 've been very kind .

56
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:53,885
On the contrary , it is entirely my privilege .

57
00:08:53,960 --> 00:08:58,284
I consider myself fortunate to have found such a distinguished scholar to act as my librarian .

58
00:08:58,360 --> 00:09:00,442
I like quiet and seclusion .

59
00:09:01,360 --> 00:09:03,567
This house , I think , offers that .

60
00:09:03,640 --> 00:09:06,211
Then we are both satisfied . An admirable arrangement .

61
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:10,684
Oh , there is just one more thing , Mr Harker .

62
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:14,321
I have to go out and I will not be back until after sundown tomorrow .

63
00:09:14,400 --> 00:09:17,882
Until then , please look upon this house as your own .

64
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:22,080
- Good night , Mr Harker . - Good night , sir .

65
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:53,010
( KNOCKING ON DOOR )

66
00:09:55,560 --> 00:09:56,656
As I shall be away for so long ,

67
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:59,376
I think it 's better that you should have the key of the library , Mr Harker .

68
00:09:59,400 --> 00:10:00,447
Thank you .

69
00:10:00,560 --> 00:10:03,040
You will find the library to the left of the hall .

70
00:10:04,880 --> 00:10:06,848
- May I ? - Yes , certainly .

71
00:10:09,640 --> 00:10:12,211
DRACULA : Your wife ? JONATHAN : No , my fiancée .

72
00:10:12,280 --> 00:10:14,200
DRACULA : You are a very fortunate man , Mr Harker .

73
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:15,881
May I ask her name ?

74
00:10:15,960 --> 00:10:18,327
Lucy . Lucy Holmwood .

75
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:22,885
- Charming , charming . - You are very kind .

76
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:27,041
Good night .

77
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:30,044
Sleep well , Mr Harker .

78
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:37,090
( DOOR LOCKING )

79
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:14,770
JONATHAN : " At last I have met Count Dracula . "

80
00:11:21,040 --> 00:11:23,884
" He accepts me as a man who has agreed "

81
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:27,887
" to work among his books , as I intended . "

82
00:11:32,920 --> 00:11:37,608
" It only remains for me now to await the daylight hours "

83
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:43,443
" when , with God 's help , " .

84
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:49,726
" I will forever end this man 's reign of terror . "

85
00:11:50,400 --> 00:11:53,051
( THUNDEROUS INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

86
00:12:39,320 --> 00:12:41,766
( SOFT , OMINOUS INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

87
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:37,565
( DOOR SHUTS LOUDLY )

88
00:13:41,360 --> 00:13:44,921
- Mr Harker , you will help me ? - If it 's at all possible .

89
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:49,290
But tell me why is Count Dracula keeping you prisoner ?

90
00:13:49,360 --> 00:13:53,968
- I cannot tell you that . - But if I am to help you , I must know .

91
00:13:54,040 --> 00:13:57,044
I 'm sorry , it 's not possible .

92
00:13:57,760 --> 00:13:59,808
You make it very difficult for me .

93
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:02,929
After all , I am a guest here . If I 'm to help you I must have a reason .

94
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:05,731
A reason . You ask for a reason !

95
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:09,122
Is it not reason enough that he keeps me locked up in this house ,

96
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:10,850
holds me against my will ?

97
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:15,124
You can have no idea what an evil man he is !

98
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:17,923
Or what terrible things he does !

99
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:23,925
I could not , dare not try to leave on my own .

100
00:14:25,360 --> 00:14:27,249
He would find me again , I know .

101
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:31,569
But with you to help me , I would have a chance .

102
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:37,288
You must help me ! You must ! You 're my only hope ! You must !

103
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:40,966
I 'll help you , I promise .

104
00:14:41,880 --> 00:14:42,927
Oh !

105
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:46,041
( SOBS )

106
00:14:46,120 --> 00:14:47,849
Please don 't distress yourself .

107
00:14:51,400 --> 00:14:52,640
Thank you .

108
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:54,971
Thank you .

109
00:14:59,760 --> 00:15:01,888
( OMINOUS INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

110
00:15:09,160 --> 00:15:10,366
( HISSES )

111
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:15,045
( WOMAN SCREAMS )

112
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:39,370
( JONATHAN CHOKING )

113
00:15:53,040 --> 00:15:54,883
( WOMAN SCREAMING )

114
00:15:58,280 --> 00:16:00,567
( CLIMACTIC INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

115
00:18:42,240 --> 00:18:46,723
" JONATHAN : " I have become a victim of Dracula and the woman in his power .

116
00:18:50,560 --> 00:18:53,564
" It may be that I am doomed to be one of them . "

117
00:18:55,040 --> 00:18:59,329
" If that is so , I can only pray "

118
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:03,042
" that whoever finds my body "

119
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:08,207
" will possess the knowledge "

120
00:19:13,120 --> 00:19:15,088
" to do what is necessary "

121
00:19:16,760 --> 00:19:18,569
" to release my soul . "

122
00:19:23,360 --> 00:19:27,206
" I have lost a day . Soon it will be dark . "

123
00:19:28,680 --> 00:19:34,369
" While my senses are still my own , I must do what I set out to do . "

124
00:19:37,680 --> 00:19:40,445
" I must find the resting place of Dracula "

125
00:19:41,760 --> 00:19:44,366
" and , there , end his existence forever . "

126
00:20:02,840 --> 00:20:06,049
" Soon it will be sundown and they will walk again . "

127
00:20:08,680 --> 00:20:10,364
" I do not have much time . "

128
00:20:37,160 --> 00:20:39,208
( DRAMATIC INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

129
00:21:35,560 --> 00:21:36,721
( WOMAN SCREAMS )

130
00:22:27,720 --> 00:22:28,767
( GASPS )

131
00:22:43,720 --> 00:22:46,929
( SUSPENSEFUL INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

132
00:22:47,360 --> 00:22:48,964
( STAKE CLATTERS )

133
00:23:11,840 --> 00:23:14,411
( LIGHT-HEARTED MUSIC-BOX MUSIC PLAYS )

134
00:23:34,160 --> 00:23:35,571
( DOOR OPENS )

135
00:23:43,560 --> 00:23:45,324
( SWITCHES OFF MUSIC )

136
00:23:46,520 --> 00:23:48,522
- Good day , sir . - Good day .

137
00:23:55,960 --> 00:23:58,964
- May I have a brandy , please ? - Certainly , sir .

138
00:24:00,200 --> 00:24:03,522
- Travelling far ? - VAN HELSING : Not much farther , I hope .

139
00:24:12,760 --> 00:24:16,606
- Is it possible to have a meal ? - Yes , sir .

140
00:24:17,160 --> 00:24:18,241
Inga !

141
00:24:18,720 --> 00:24:21,200
Only a simple one , I 'm afraid , sir .

142
00:24:25,560 --> 00:24:27,369
- Your change , sir . - Thank you .

143
00:24:28,040 --> 00:24:32,204
We don 't get many travellers in these parts . Not that stop , anyway .

144
00:24:32,880 --> 00:24:35,884
You had one a few days ago , I believe . A Mr Harker .

145
00:24:37,280 --> 00:24:39,123
- Harker , sir ? - Yes .

146
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:41,045
He 's a friend of mine .

147
00:24:41,120 --> 00:24:44,329
- He wrote to me from this address . - Not here , sir .

148
00:24:44,600 --> 00:24:47,649
I remember the gentleman . He gave me a letter to post .

149
00:24:47,720 --> 00:24:49,165
Hold your tongue , girl !

150
00:24:49,240 --> 00:24:50,526
Was this the letter ?

151
00:24:52,720 --> 00:24:54,961
- I 'm not sure . - Perhaps you remember the name .

152
00:24:55,040 --> 00:24:56,565
Dr Van Helsing .

153
00:24:57,680 --> 00:24:58,886
I 'm not sure .

154
00:24:58,960 --> 00:25:03,045
Go and prepare a meal for this gentleman . At once . Do you hear me ?

155
00:25:08,600 --> 00:25:10,045
What are you afraid of ?

156
00:25:11,720 --> 00:25:15,122
- I don 't understand you . - Why all these garlic flowers ?

157
00:25:15,200 --> 00:25:16,804
And over the window ?

158
00:25:22,760 --> 00:25:23,921
And up here ?

159
00:25:25,560 --> 00:25:27,528
They 're not for decoration , are they ?

160
00:25:27,600 --> 00:25:30,649
- I don 't know what you 're talking about . - I think you do .

161
00:25:30,720 --> 00:25:32,560
And I think you know something about my friend .

162
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:35,606
He came here with a purpose , to help you .

163
00:25:35,680 --> 00:25:36,880
We haven 't asked for any help .

164
00:25:37,320 --> 00:25:38,367
You need it all the same .

165
00:25:39,280 --> 00:25:42,523
Look , sir , you 're a stranger here in Klausenburg .

166
00:25:43,040 --> 00:25:44,963
Some things are best left alone ,

167
00:25:45,560 --> 00:25:48,643
such as interfering in things which are beyond our powers .

168
00:25:49,040 --> 00:25:51,247
Please don 't misunderstand me .

169
00:25:51,320 --> 00:25:55,211
This is more than a superstition . I know . The danger is very real .

170
00:25:55,840 --> 00:25:58,730
If the investigation that Mr Harker and I are engaged upon is successful

171
00:25:59,360 --> 00:26:01,442
not only you , but the whole world will benefit .

172
00:26:02,320 --> 00:26:05,051
VAN HELSING : Castle Dracula is somewhere here in Klausenburg .

173
00:26:05,320 --> 00:26:07,641
Will you tell me how I get there ?

174
00:26:07,720 --> 00:26:11,691
You ordered a meal , sir . As an innkeeper , it is my duty to serve you .

175
00:26:12,440 --> 00:26:16,161
When you have eaten , I ask you to go and leave us in peace .

176
00:26:16,240 --> 00:26:20,609
Your meal will be ready in a minute , sir , if you 'd like to take a seat .

177
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:22,331
Thank you .

178
00:26:35,000 --> 00:26:37,810
This was found at the crossroads near that place .

179
00:26:37,880 --> 00:26:39,609
He told me to burn it .

180
00:26:39,680 --> 00:26:42,763
But your friend was such a nice gentleman , I couldn 't .

181
00:27:48,880 --> 00:27:50,086
Harker ?

182
00:28:02,120 --> 00:28:03,326
Harker !

183
00:28:09,560 --> 00:28:10,607
Harker !

184
00:28:18,920 --> 00:28:20,126
Harker !

185
00:29:05,080 --> 00:29:07,287
( SINISTER INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

186
00:29:48,360 --> 00:29:50,601
( CLIMACTIC INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

187
00:30:09,520 --> 00:30:11,090
( METAL CLINKING )

188
00:30:33,080 --> 00:30:36,801
I 'm sorry , Mr Holmwood , but I really can not tell you anything more about how he died .

189
00:30:37,120 --> 00:30:38,884
Can not or will not ?

190
00:30:39,240 --> 00:30:40,924
Whichever you wish .

191
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:43,526
Dr Van Helsing , I am not at all satisfied .

192
00:30:44,880 --> 00:30:48,771
You suddenly appear and tell us that Jonathan Harker is dead .

193
00:30:48,840 --> 00:30:51,844
Yet you will not tell us where or how he died .

194
00:30:51,920 --> 00:30:54,730
- I find it extremely suspicious . - Arthur !

195
00:30:55,360 --> 00:30:59,649
- You have the death certificate . - Yes . Signed by you .

196
00:31:00,240 --> 00:31:02,288
When did he die , Doctor ?

197
00:31:02,360 --> 00:31:05,091
- 10 days ago , Mrs Holmwood . - 10 days ago !

198
00:31:05,640 --> 00:31:08,166
- Where was he buried ? - He was cremated .

199
00:31:08,680 --> 00:31:10,887
- By whose authority ? - His own .

200
00:31:11,920 --> 00:31:14,920
As his friend and colleague , he told me some time ago that he would wish it .

201
00:31:18,080 --> 00:31:21,687
You must know that Jonathan was going to marry my sister Lucy .

202
00:31:21,760 --> 00:31:23,728
Surely you could have written .

203
00:31:23,800 --> 00:31:28,044
I felt it would have been less of a shock if I came and told her personally .

204
00:31:28,120 --> 00:31:30,885
I would rather you didn 't see my sister .

205
00:31:31,560 --> 00:31:33,722
My wife and I will tell her .

206
00:31:34,560 --> 00:31:36,881
Very well . I 'm sorry .

207
00:31:37,680 --> 00:31:40,331
Will you please express my sympathy to Miss Lucy ?

208
00:31:40,400 --> 00:31:44,121
If she wishes to get in touch with me , I am at her service .

209
00:31:45,520 --> 00:31:49,127
Oh , Gerda , Dr Van Helsing is leaving . Will you show him to the door ?

210
00:31:49,200 --> 00:31:50,247
Yes , sir .

211
00:31:50,320 --> 00:31:51,845
Good day . Sir .

212
00:32:02,880 --> 00:32:05,963
Why all this secrecy ? Why wouldn 't he tell us ?

213
00:32:06,040 --> 00:32:09,840
Darling , Dr Van Helsing is a very eminent man .

214
00:32:11,520 --> 00:32:14,922
Whatever his motives , you can be sure he had a good reason for them .

215
00:32:16,160 --> 00:32:18,731
In any case , we can 't help poor Jonathan now .

216
00:32:19,840 --> 00:32:21,968
Lucy is the one we must think of .

217
00:32:23,400 --> 00:32:25,687
Is she well enough to be told ?

218
00:32:26,280 --> 00:32:30,080
- It will be a terrible blow for her . - She must know sometime .

219
00:32:31,640 --> 00:32:35,042
We won 't disturb her afternoon rest . We 'll see how she is this evening .

220
00:32:36,200 --> 00:32:40,649
Jonathan will be home soon , I know it . Then I 'll get better , you 'll see .

221
00:32:40,720 --> 00:32:43,451
I won 't be a trouble to Dr Seward or any of you .

222
00:32:43,560 --> 00:32:47,610
Lucy , you 're no trouble to anyone . Now rest , get some sleep .

223
00:32:48,560 --> 00:32:51,723
You 've got to get some colour back into those cheeks .

224
00:32:51,800 --> 00:32:54,326
- Good night , Lucy . - Good night , Mina .

225
00:32:54,720 --> 00:32:56,131
Good night , Arthur .

226
00:32:57,560 --> 00:32:59,562
( SOFT INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

227
00:33:14,520 --> 00:33:16,887
- MINA : Sleep well . - I 'll try .

228
00:33:21,280 --> 00:33:23,567
( EERIE INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

229
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:30,287
( FOREBODING INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

230
00:34:38,200 --> 00:34:40,123
HELSING : ( ON GRAMOPHONE ) Research on vampires .

231
00:34:40,200 --> 00:34:43,010
Certain basic facts established .

232
00:34:43,520 --> 00:34:45,045
One , light .

233
00:34:46,040 --> 00:34:48,407
The vampire allergic to light .

234
00:34:49,120 --> 00:34:51,964
Never ventures forth in the daytime .

235
00:34:52,800 --> 00:34:56,247
Sunlight , fatal . Repeat , fatal .

236
00:34:57,240 --> 00:34:59,129
Would destroy them .

237
00:34:59,800 --> 00:35:01,928
Two , garlic .

238
00:35:03,120 --> 00:35:06,602
Vampires repelled by odor of garlic .

239
00:35:08,360 --> 00:35:12,160
Memo . Check final arrangements with Harker before he leaves for Klausenburg .

240
00:35:13,920 --> 00:35:16,890
Three , the crucifix .

241
00:35:17,600 --> 00:35:21,082
Symbolizing the power of good over evil .

242
00:35:21,160 --> 00:35:22,366
( KNOCKING ON DOOR )

243
00:35:22,440 --> 00:35:25,728
The power of the crucifix in these cases ...

244
00:35:26,720 --> 00:35:27,960
Come in .

245
00:35:29,840 --> 00:35:32,411
- You rang , sir ? - Oh , yes .

246
00:35:33,200 --> 00:35:35,771
I want this letter delivered first thing in the morning .

247
00:35:35,840 --> 00:35:38,889
- Will you see to that ? - Yes .

248
00:35:38,960 --> 00:35:41,247
- Thank you . - Thank you , sir .

249
00:35:44,600 --> 00:35:46,170
Anything the matter ?

250
00:35:47,000 --> 00:35:48,331
What is it ?

251
00:35:48,400 --> 00:35:53,406
To tell you the truth , when I was outside , I thought I heard you talking to someone .

252
00:35:53,880 --> 00:35:58,647
Of course you did . I was talking to myself . You won 't forget that letter , will you ?

253
00:35:58,720 --> 00:36:00,006
No , sir .

254
00:36:01,120 --> 00:36:02,201
Yes .

255
00:36:18,840 --> 00:36:23,448
HELSING : ( ON GRAMOPHONE ) The power of the crucifix in these cases is two-fold .

256
00:36:24,880 --> 00:36:27,929
It protects the normal human being ,

257
00:36:28,560 --> 00:36:31,928
but reveals the vampire or victim

258
00:36:32,400 --> 00:36:37,122
of this vile contagion when in advanced stages .

259
00:36:57,040 --> 00:37:03,207
Established that victims consciously detest being dominated by vampirism

260
00:37:03,880 --> 00:37:07,805
but are unable to relinquish the practice ,

261
00:37:08,680 --> 00:37:11,524
similar to addiction to drugs .

262
00:37:12,800 --> 00:37:16,646
Ultimately , death results from loss of blood .

263
00:37:17,560 --> 00:37:22,088
But , unlike normal death , no peace manifests itself

264
00:37:23,240 --> 00:37:27,325
for they enter into the fearful state of the undead .

265
00:37:29,160 --> 00:37:33,006
Since the death of Jonathan Harker , Count Dracula ,

266
00:37:33,680 --> 00:37:37,730
the propagator of this unspeakable evil , has disappeared .

267
00:37:39,040 --> 00:37:42,442
He must be found and destroyed .

268
00:37:42,880 --> 00:37:45,042
( DRAMATIC INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

269
00:38:16,720 --> 00:38:18,927
( CLIMACTIC INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

270
00:38:27,880 --> 00:38:32,329
- She seems so much weaker , Doctor . - It 's a puzzling case , Mrs Holmwood .

271
00:38:32,400 --> 00:38:35,768
The symptoms are those of anemia and I 'm treating her for this .

272
00:38:35,840 --> 00:38:38,366
It can be a slow process , of course .

273
00:38:38,440 --> 00:38:40,886
I had hoped for more encouraging signs by now .

274
00:38:40,960 --> 00:38:43,964
- Please may I see Auntie Lucy ? - Not today , Tania .

275
00:38:44,320 --> 00:38:46,766
- Is she very ill ? - I 'm afraid so .

276
00:38:47,200 --> 00:38:50,409
- Do you know what 's wrong with her ? - Of course I do .

277
00:38:50,520 --> 00:38:52,284
Then why don 't you make her better ?

278
00:38:52,840 --> 00:38:54,968
Tania . Tania !

279
00:38:55,560 --> 00:38:58,848
How many times have I told you not to go bothering Mrs Holmwood ?

280
00:38:58,920 --> 00:39:01,844
- I 'm sorry , ma 'am . - That 's all right , Gerda .

281
00:39:02,880 --> 00:39:07,363
- A child 's logic can be most disconcerting . - Yes .

282
00:39:09,560 --> 00:39:11,927
Would you like a second opinion , Mrs Holmwood ?

283
00:39:13,520 --> 00:39:15,841
Thank you , Doctor . I 'll think about it .

284
00:39:17,000 --> 00:39:20,561
Well , carry on with the medicine and diet I 've prescribed

285
00:39:21,120 --> 00:39:23,930
- and plenty of fresh air . - Yes , Doctor , I will .

286
00:39:25,680 --> 00:39:28,365
MINA : Good day to you . SEWARD : Good day .

287
00:39:43,280 --> 00:39:44,805
( KNOCKING ON DOOR )

288
00:39:44,880 --> 00:39:46,086
Come in .

289
00:39:48,200 --> 00:39:50,680
Mrs Holmwood , how very good of you to come .

290
00:39:50,760 --> 00:39:54,207
- Please , will you sit down ? - Thank you .

291
00:39:57,080 --> 00:39:59,606
You mentioned in your letter some things of Jonathan 's .

292
00:39:59,680 --> 00:40:02,809
Yes , I have them ready . I would have brought them myself , but ...

293
00:40:02,880 --> 00:40:07,408
Oh , I do understand . But you must appreciate Mr Holmwood was very upset .

294
00:40:07,520 --> 00:40:08,806
Of course .

295
00:40:08,880 --> 00:40:11,770
I only wish I could have been more helpful .

296
00:40:11,840 --> 00:40:14,161
How did Miss Lucy take the news ?

297
00:40:14,360 --> 00:40:18,046
We haven 't told her yet . Oh , she 's ill , very ill .

298
00:40:18,400 --> 00:40:21,768
I 'm sorry to hear that . May I ask what 's the matter with her ?

299
00:40:23,240 --> 00:40:27,040
It was all so sudden . It happened about 10 days ago .

300
00:40:28,240 --> 00:40:30,811
Our family doctor says it 's anaemia .

301
00:40:31,640 --> 00:40:32,926
But I 'm very unhappy about it .

302
00:40:33,600 --> 00:40:37,082
Oh , I have nothing against Dr Seward , please don 't think that , but ...

303
00:40:37,720 --> 00:40:41,645
- He did say I could have a second opinion . - I 'd like to see her at once .

304
00:40:42,560 --> 00:40:45,848
- Oh ! I 'd be so grateful . - If you 'll excuse me .

305
00:40:49,360 --> 00:40:52,443
MINA : Lucy , I 've brought someone to see you .

306
00:40:52,560 --> 00:40:55,211
Dr Van Helsing . He 's a friend of Jonathan 's .

307
00:40:55,280 --> 00:40:56,645
Miss Lucy .

308
00:41:00,320 --> 00:41:01,367
What lovely flowers .

309
00:41:03,000 --> 00:41:04,525
Jonathan 's dead , isn 't he ?

310
00:41:05,680 --> 00:41:09,127
- It 's true , isn 't it ? - I 'm sorry .

311
00:41:09,560 --> 00:41:13,724
- MINA : Did Arthur tell you ? - Nobody told me . I just knew .

312
00:41:14,640 --> 00:41:17,450
- Is that why Dr Helsing is here ? - Partly .

313
00:41:17,880 --> 00:41:20,281
Dr Helsing is a specialist . He 's come to help you .

314
00:41:21,360 --> 00:41:24,091
Jonathan has told me so many things about you .

315
00:41:24,160 --> 00:41:26,640
- Well , nice things , I hope . - Very nice .

316
00:41:27,640 --> 00:41:28,926
Now , let 's see .

317
00:41:30,640 --> 00:41:31,880
Mmm-hmm .

318
00:41:33,880 --> 00:41:35,166
And here .

319
00:41:44,520 --> 00:41:47,808
Now don 't you worry , we 'll soon have you well again .

320
00:41:48,440 --> 00:41:50,124
Good bye , Doctor .

321
00:41:50,200 --> 00:41:53,727
I 'm sorry you had a wasted journey , about Jonathan , I mean .

322
00:41:54,200 --> 00:41:57,522
It wasn 't wasted , I promise you . Good day , Miss Lucy .

323
00:42:07,040 --> 00:42:09,930
How could she have known of Jonathan 's death ?

324
00:42:10,000 --> 00:42:14,688
- A premonition . It 's not uncommon . - But she took it so calmly , it worries me .

325
00:42:14,760 --> 00:42:17,161
I 'm afraid there are more urgent things to worry about .

326
00:42:17,240 --> 00:42:20,084
Those marks on her neck , when did they first appear ?

327
00:42:20,160 --> 00:42:22,606
I noticed them first shortly after she became ill .

328
00:42:22,680 --> 00:42:25,206
I asked her about them . She said she thought she had been stung .

329
00:42:25,840 --> 00:42:27,365
Well , it is quite possible , of course .

330
00:42:27,440 --> 00:42:32,082
Dr Seward said she must have plenty of fresh air . Her windows are open all the time .

331
00:42:32,160 --> 00:42:35,130
Between the hours of sunset and sunrise , all the windows in her room ,

332
00:42:35,200 --> 00:42:39,444
with the possible exception of a small fanlight for ventilation , must be kept shut .

333
00:42:39,560 --> 00:42:41,449
- Oh , but Dr Seward said ... - Mrs Holmwood ,

334
00:42:41,560 --> 00:42:43,449
you called me in for a second opinion .

335
00:42:44,040 --> 00:42:47,360
If I am to help your sister-in-law , there are certain things you must do to help me ,

336
00:42:48,200 --> 00:42:49,964
however unorthodox they may appear .

337
00:42:50,040 --> 00:42:51,280
- Yes , I know , but ... - Madam ...

338
00:42:53,120 --> 00:42:57,205
If you love Miss Lucy , be guided by me , I beg you .

339
00:42:58,520 --> 00:43:01,126
I 'll do anything to make her well again .

340
00:43:01,200 --> 00:43:06,127
Now , you must get some garlic flowers , as many as you can .

341
00:43:06,600 --> 00:43:10,286
Place them by her windows , and her door and by her bedside .

342
00:43:10,360 --> 00:43:13,569
They may be taken out during the day , but under no circumstances ,

343
00:43:13,640 --> 00:43:17,440
even if the patient implores you , must they be removed at night .

344
00:43:20,560 --> 00:43:22,210
I cannot impress upon you strongly enough

345
00:43:22,280 --> 00:43:25,409
how important it is that you obey my instructions .

346
00:43:25,520 --> 00:43:28,763
Do exactly as I say and we may be able to save her .

347
00:43:28,840 --> 00:43:31,207
If you don 't , she will die .

348
00:43:33,720 --> 00:43:35,882
I 'll be here in the morning .

349
00:43:44,720 --> 00:43:46,210
( LUCY MOANING )

350
00:43:47,200 --> 00:43:49,043
( PANTING )

351
00:43:51,360 --> 00:43:54,125
( MOANING )

352
00:44:04,720 --> 00:44:06,722
( VASE SHATTERS )

353
00:44:09,080 --> 00:44:11,048
Heavens , child ! What is it ?

354
00:44:12,040 --> 00:44:15,761
Oh , Gerda . These flowers , I can 't stand them !

355
00:44:15,840 --> 00:44:18,241
They do smell strongly , but Mrs Holmwood said ...

356
00:44:18,320 --> 00:44:21,642
I don 't care what she said ! Please , take them away ! Please !

357
00:44:21,720 --> 00:44:22,801
Well ...

358
00:44:22,880 --> 00:44:26,043
Oh , please , Gerda , they stifle me .

359
00:44:28,760 --> 00:44:31,650
All right , miss , I 'll take them out .

360
00:44:31,720 --> 00:44:34,451
And the windows , you 'll open the windows ?

361
00:44:34,560 --> 00:44:37,291
Yes , Miss Lucy , if that 's what you want .

362
00:44:56,720 --> 00:44:58,882
I 'll come back for the rest .

363
00:45:10,560 --> 00:45:12,881
( FOREBODING INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

364
00:45:30,040 --> 00:45:31,849
There was nothing I could do to save her .

365
00:45:32,360 --> 00:45:34,727
- ( KNOCKING ON DOOR ) - ( DOOR OPENS )

366
00:45:57,200 --> 00:45:58,850
SEWARD : Doctor Van ...

367
00:46:02,880 --> 00:46:05,611
Mrs Holmwood , did you do as I told you ?

368
00:46:06,000 --> 00:46:08,651
She did . And you have seen the result .

369
00:46:09,000 --> 00:46:12,049
- But , Arthur ... - Please , sir . Excuse me , sir .

370
00:46:12,320 --> 00:46:16,769
It was all my fault . She could not breathe . She looked so ill .

371
00:46:16,840 --> 00:46:19,730
She begged me to open the windows and throw away all the plants .

372
00:46:19,800 --> 00:46:21,536
Oh , I know you told me not to , ma 'am , but ...

373
00:46:21,560 --> 00:46:23,403
Gerda , what time was this ?

374
00:46:25,320 --> 00:46:26,526
It was about midnight .

375
00:46:27,840 --> 00:46:29,720
- I heard a noise ... - ARTHUR : All right , Gerda .

376
00:46:30,160 --> 00:46:33,004
- You may go now . - Yes , sir . Thank you , sir .

377
00:46:33,520 --> 00:46:35,568
Oh , I am so sorry , sir .

378
00:46:39,320 --> 00:46:42,881
Whatever happened , all I know is that you have brought us nothing but grief .

379
00:46:43,360 --> 00:46:45,442
First Jonathan , and now Lucy .

380
00:46:46,120 --> 00:46:50,887
Whoever you are and whatever your motives , please go and leave us in peace .

381
00:46:53,200 --> 00:46:56,283
Mr Holmwood , when I told you about Jonathan ,

382
00:46:56,360 --> 00:46:58,886
I thought it better for your peace of mind to spare the details

383
00:46:58,960 --> 00:47:00,962
of the dreadful circumstances in which he died .

384
00:47:02,520 --> 00:47:06,605
But the tragic death of your sister is so closely linked with Jonathan 's

385
00:47:06,680 --> 00:47:08,569
that I think you should now know the truth .

386
00:47:09,000 --> 00:47:12,721
I can 't expect you to believe me , but you will , I know , believe Jonathan .

387
00:47:14,360 --> 00:47:17,170
Here are his last words . His diary .

388
00:47:17,960 --> 00:47:20,884
When you have read it , you will understand .

389
00:47:47,680 --> 00:47:48,936
ARTHUR : Well , what is it , Gerda ?

390
00:47:48,960 --> 00:47:52,123
It 's a policeman , sir . He 's got Tania with him .

391
00:47:52,200 --> 00:47:53,361
Tania ?

392
00:47:54,000 --> 00:47:56,401
- Show him in , Gerda . - Very good , sir .

393
00:48:02,320 --> 00:48:05,449
- Good evening , ma 'am . Good evening , sir . - What is it , officer ?

394
00:48:05,880 --> 00:48:09,805
I found this little girl , here . She was very distressed indeed .

395
00:48:10,520 --> 00:48:13,763
- Tell them what you told me . - I don 't want to .

396
00:48:14,280 --> 00:48:15,327
Oh ...

397
00:48:16,280 --> 00:48:17,441
Tania !

398
00:48:18,600 --> 00:48:21,001
There 's no need to be frightened .

399
00:48:21,080 --> 00:48:24,926
Now , come on over here , sit with me , and tell me all about it .

400
00:48:25,000 --> 00:48:26,047
Oh .

401
00:48:26,400 --> 00:48:29,927
Now , you don 't want Mr Holmwood to think you 're a crybaby , do you ?

402
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:31,889
You 're a big girl now .

403
00:48:32,120 --> 00:48:34,691
Now , come on . Tell me what happened .

404
00:48:35,040 --> 00:48:39,841
Well , I was out by myself , and she came up to me .

405
00:48:40,360 --> 00:48:44,126
And she said , " Hello , Tania , shall we go for a little walk ? "

406
00:48:44,680 --> 00:48:47,809
And I said yes . And we went for a walk .

407
00:48:48,120 --> 00:48:51,806
Then someone came along , and she ran away and left me

408
00:48:51,880 --> 00:48:53,803
and I was lost .

409
00:48:54,840 --> 00:48:57,320
Who was she ? Who did you see ?

410
00:48:59,040 --> 00:49:00,804
Come on . Tell me .

411
00:49:01,560 --> 00:49:02,925
Who was she ?

412
00:49:04,280 --> 00:49:05,725
Aunt Lucy .

413
00:49:05,880 --> 00:49:08,087
( DRAMATIC INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

414
00:49:56,320 --> 00:49:58,641
( FOREBODING INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

415
00:50:28,560 --> 00:50:32,201
- I heard you call me , Aunt Lucy . - Yes , dear .

416
00:50:36,360 --> 00:50:37,725
Come along .

417
00:50:39,040 --> 00:50:41,964
You 're cold . Where are we going ?

418
00:50:42,040 --> 00:50:46,250
For a little walk . I know somewhere nice and quiet where we can play .

419
00:51:19,880 --> 00:51:24,010
Is it much further , Aunt Lucy ? I 'm so tired .

420
00:51:24,440 --> 00:51:26,761
We 're nearly there , my darling .

421
00:51:26,840 --> 00:51:27,887
Lucy !

422
00:51:33,800 --> 00:51:35,450
Arthur , dear brother !

423
00:51:35,800 --> 00:51:36,881
Lucy !

424
00:51:37,560 --> 00:51:40,564
Dear Arthur , why didn 't you come sooner ?

425
00:51:43,200 --> 00:51:45,680
Come , let me kiss you .

426
00:51:45,760 --> 00:51:47,569
( GASPING )

427
00:51:54,560 --> 00:51:56,130
( SCREAMING )

428
00:52:22,000 --> 00:52:23,365
Put this on .

429
00:52:25,360 --> 00:52:28,921
- Please , I want to go home . - And so you shall .

430
00:52:29,880 --> 00:52:32,850
I 'll just go and fetch Mr Holmwood and then we can all go home together .

431
00:52:32,920 --> 00:52:37,050
- Not Aunt Lucy . - No , not Aunt Lucy . Now you sit here .

432
00:52:37,920 --> 00:52:39,968
Be a good girl . There .

433
00:52:40,560 --> 00:52:44,531
You look like a teddy bear now . Will you wear this pretty thing ?

434
00:52:46,040 --> 00:52:48,361
There . Isn 't that lovely ?

435
00:52:49,200 --> 00:52:51,965
- Now , you promise not to run away ? - I promise .

436
00:52:52,040 --> 00:52:53,804
Good . Now , look ,

437
00:52:54,880 --> 00:52:58,202
if you watch over there , you 'll see the sun come up .

438
00:53:00,240 --> 00:53:01,605
Keep warm .

439
00:53:18,440 --> 00:53:20,204
You understand now ?

440
00:53:22,600 --> 00:53:25,365
- But why Lucy ? - Because of Jonathan .

441
00:53:26,200 --> 00:53:29,807
You read my note in his diary about the woman he found at Klausenburg .

442
00:53:29,880 --> 00:53:32,042
This is Dracula 's revenge .

443
00:53:32,120 --> 00:53:34,930
- Lucy is to replace that woman . - Oh , no !

444
00:53:35,000 --> 00:53:39,164
I 've watched her tomb each night since she was interred three days ago .

445
00:53:39,240 --> 00:53:42,130
Tonight she ventured out for the first time .

446
00:53:42,200 --> 00:53:46,285
Holmwood , I know your one wish is that Lucy should rest in peace .

447
00:53:46,360 --> 00:53:49,648
I promise to fulfill that wish . But , first ,

448
00:53:50,120 --> 00:53:53,567
if I have your consent , she can lead us to Dracula .

449
00:53:54,880 --> 00:53:57,247
How can you suggest such a thing ?

450
00:53:57,640 --> 00:54:01,406
That she should be possessed by this evil for another second ?

451
00:54:02,240 --> 00:54:06,609
And what about Gerda 's child out there , and the others she will defile ?

452
00:54:07,040 --> 00:54:09,520
Oh , no , I couldn 't ! I couldn 't !

453
00:54:16,720 --> 00:54:18,051
Of course .

454
00:54:18,560 --> 00:54:23,407
Will you take that child home and then meet me back here in about an hour 's time ?

455
00:54:23,520 --> 00:54:24,726
It 's all right .

456
00:54:24,800 --> 00:54:28,043
It 's nearly dawn , she won 't leave the coffin again .

457
00:54:41,000 --> 00:54:42,889
Is there no other way ?

458
00:54:44,080 --> 00:54:45,764
But it 's horrible !

459
00:54:46,960 --> 00:54:49,008
Please try and understand .

460
00:54:49,400 --> 00:54:52,927
This is not Lucy , the sister you loved . It 's only a shell .

461
00:54:53,000 --> 00:54:55,924
Possessed and corrupted by the evil of Dracula !

462
00:54:56,000 --> 00:55:01,564
To liberate her soul and give it eternal peace , we must destroy that shell for all time !

463
00:55:03,880 --> 00:55:06,326
Believe me , there is no other way .

464
00:55:30,880 --> 00:55:32,006
( SCREAMING )

465
00:55:37,200 --> 00:55:38,247
( MOANING )

466
00:56:49,880 --> 00:56:52,281
- Drink this . - Oh , I 'm all right now .

467
00:56:52,360 --> 00:56:55,011
- Drink it . - Thanks .

468
00:57:00,680 --> 00:57:04,127
There 's so much in Jonathan 's diary I don 't understand .

469
00:57:04,560 --> 00:57:07,564
Can Dracula really be as old as it says here ?

470
00:57:07,640 --> 00:57:09,210
We believe it 's possible .

471
00:57:09,280 --> 00:57:12,045
Vampires are known to have gone on from century to century .

472
00:57:12,120 --> 00:57:15,966
Records show that Count Dracula could be 500 or 600 years old .

473
00:57:17,840 --> 00:57:19,251
Another thing .

474
00:57:19,320 --> 00:57:22,449
I always understood that , if there were such things ,

475
00:57:22,560 --> 00:57:25,723
they could change themselves into bats or wolves .

476
00:57:27,000 --> 00:57:28,968
That 's a common fallacy .

477
00:57:29,560 --> 00:57:33,565
Holmwood , the study of these creatures has been my life 's work .

478
00:57:34,040 --> 00:57:36,816
I 've carried out research with some of the greatest authorities in Europe .

479
00:57:36,840 --> 00:57:39,366
And yet , we 've only just scratched the surface .

480
00:57:39,440 --> 00:57:42,364
You see , a great deal is known about the vampire bat .

481
00:57:42,440 --> 00:57:46,047
But details of these re-animated bodies of the dead ,

482
00:57:46,120 --> 00:57:48,248
the " undead , " as we call them ,

483
00:57:48,320 --> 00:57:52,325
are so obscure , that many biologists will not believe they exist .

484
00:57:54,800 --> 00:57:57,644
Of course , you are shocked and bewildered .

485
00:57:57,720 --> 00:58:00,849
How can you expect to understand in so short a time ?

486
00:58:00,920 --> 00:58:03,810
But you 've read and experienced enough to know

487
00:58:03,880 --> 00:58:06,645
that this unholy cult must be wiped out .

488
00:58:07,640 --> 00:58:11,850
- I hope perhaps that you will help me . - I 'll do anything you say .

489
00:58:12,720 --> 00:58:14,051
Thank you .

490
00:58:14,600 --> 00:58:17,206
Of course , we do know certain things .

491
00:58:17,680 --> 00:58:20,251
You witnessed one a little while ago .

492
00:58:20,320 --> 00:58:25,770
And we also know that during the day the vampire must rest in his native soil .

493
00:58:26,560 --> 00:58:27,607
Now .

494
00:58:28,400 --> 00:58:32,041
When I went to Castle Dracula , a hearse came tearing through the gates .

495
00:58:32,160 --> 00:58:34,128
In that hearse was a coffin .

496
00:58:34,200 --> 00:58:37,204
I believe it contained Dracula and a bed of his own earth .

497
00:58:37,600 --> 00:58:41,571
To get here , that hearse would have to come via the frontier at Ingstadt .

498
00:58:41,640 --> 00:58:43,600
They 'll have a record there of where it was going .

499
00:58:43,720 --> 00:58:47,406
We need that address . Will you come with me to Ingstadt ?

500
00:58:50,720 --> 00:58:53,121
How long will it take ? I must let Mina know .

501
00:58:53,200 --> 00:58:56,204
With any luck , we should be back by tomorrow morning .

502
00:59:03,760 --> 00:59:05,091
( COUGHING )

503
00:59:06,880 --> 00:59:10,282
I 'm afraid that is quite out of the question , sir . Against regulations .

504
00:59:10,360 --> 00:59:12,328
All we want to know is where the coffin was going .

505
00:59:12,400 --> 00:59:15,370
I can 't give away information without proper authority .

506
00:59:15,440 --> 00:59:17,727
This is a matter of great urgency ! I am a doctor .

507
00:59:17,800 --> 00:59:19,040
I 'm sorry , sir .

508
00:59:20,280 --> 00:59:22,726
There 's a young lad with a message for you .

509
00:59:22,800 --> 00:59:24,723
Personal , he said . He wouldn 't give it to me .

510
00:59:24,800 --> 00:59:26,564
All right , Gerda , I 'll see him .

511
00:59:36,960 --> 00:59:38,962
- Yes ? - You Mrs Holmwood ?

512
00:59:39,040 --> 00:59:41,122
- I am . - Got a message for you .

513
00:59:41,200 --> 00:59:44,010
You 're to go to 49 Frederickstrasse right away , he says .

514
00:59:44,080 --> 00:59:45,650
And you 're not to tell anyone .

515
00:59:45,720 --> 00:59:46,767
Who says ?

516
00:59:47,040 --> 00:59:49,884
Arthur Holmwood , he calls himself . Said you 'd know him .

517
00:59:50,560 --> 00:59:53,291
But that 's impossible . My husband has gone to Ingstadt .

518
00:59:53,360 --> 00:59:56,762
Not if he gave me this message , he hasn 't . And he gave me this message .

519
00:59:56,840 --> 00:59:58,205
Good night .

520
01:00:01,040 --> 01:00:03,407
You 've got to have permission from the Ministry in writing .

521
01:00:03,520 --> 01:00:06,171
I have my orders and I must obey them .

522
01:00:06,240 --> 01:00:11,007
It is laid down in the government regulations that under no circumstances ...

523
01:00:13,040 --> 01:00:17,762
Under no circumstances may an unauthorized person be permitted to examine .

524
01:00:20,040 --> 01:00:24,523
Of course , in the case of an emergency , we do sometimes make an exception .

525
01:00:24,600 --> 01:00:27,285
And seeing this gentleman is a doctor ...

526
01:00:27,360 --> 01:00:28,725
( COUGHING )

527
01:00:32,120 --> 01:00:34,691
- When did you say it was , sir ? - December 1 .

528
01:00:34,760 --> 01:00:39,322
December 1 . Klausenburg to Karlstadt . Let me see .

529
01:00:41,440 --> 01:00:44,364
Here it is . One hearse , one coffin .

530
01:00:45,120 --> 01:00:49,444
J. Marx , 49 Frederickstrasse , Karlstadt .

531
01:00:52,840 --> 01:00:54,524
( RINGING DOORBELL )

532
01:01:12,600 --> 01:01:14,045
MINA : Arthur ?

533
01:01:23,200 --> 01:01:24,406
Arthur ?

534
01:01:26,800 --> 01:01:29,121
( SUSPENSEFUL INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

535
01:01:50,800 --> 01:01:53,690
Are you sure I can 't get you anything to eat , sir ?

536
01:01:54,560 --> 01:01:56,403
No , thank you , Gerda . We haven 't time .

537
01:01:56,520 --> 01:01:59,364
But I would like a word with Mrs Holmwood before we go .

538
01:01:59,440 --> 01:02:02,887
- Will you go up and see if she 's awake yet ? - Yes , sir .

539
01:02:12,200 --> 01:02:13,725
Are you ready ?

540
01:02:23,280 --> 01:02:25,886
- She 's not there , sir . - Not there ?

541
01:02:25,960 --> 01:02:27,405
GERDA : No , sir .

542
01:02:27,520 --> 01:02:28,601
MINA : Good morning .

543
01:02:32,720 --> 01:02:35,291
Mina , you gave me quite a fright .

544
01:02:35,360 --> 01:02:37,240
Where have you been at this hour of the morning ?

545
01:02:37,280 --> 01:02:41,001
It was such a lovely day , I got up early and went for a walk in the garden .

546
01:02:41,080 --> 01:02:44,801
- I didn 't expect you back so soon . - I 'm afraid I 've to go out again .

547
01:02:44,880 --> 01:02:48,601
- Oh . When will you be back ? - I can 't say for sure .

548
01:02:50,120 --> 01:02:52,851
Mina , you look pale . Are you all right ?

549
01:02:53,440 --> 01:02:56,762
Arthur , darling , don 't fuss . I feel perfectly well .

550
01:02:58,520 --> 01:03:00,124
Goodbye , darling .

551
01:03:06,040 --> 01:03:08,566
( DOOR OPENS AND CLOSES )

552
01:03:32,720 --> 01:03:37,931
Perhaps you 'd better let me lead the way , I know these steps , they can be dangerous .

553
01:03:38,000 --> 01:03:42,244
We don 't want to have an accident , do we ? No , we don 't .

554
01:03:43,560 --> 01:03:46,404
You know , an old man came here once to see his dear departed

555
01:03:46,520 --> 01:03:50,445
and he fell down these stairs . ( LAUGHS ) It was quite amusing .

556
01:03:50,560 --> 01:03:55,009
He came to pay his last respects and he remained to share them .

557
01:03:55,080 --> 01:03:57,367
( LAUGHING ) Oh , quite amusing .

558
01:03:59,160 --> 01:04:02,289
Where are we ? Where are we ? Where are we ?

559
01:04:03,560 --> 01:04:05,847
It 's around the back , somewhere .

560
01:04:05,920 --> 01:04:08,651
It 's been here so long it 's bound to be at the back , isn 't it ?

561
01:04:08,720 --> 01:04:11,246
Come on , this way , gentlemen . You follow me .

562
01:04:11,960 --> 01:04:14,201
I know where it was . This way .

563
01:04:17,800 --> 01:04:19,689
There 's an extraordinary thing !

564
01:04:20,400 --> 01:04:24,200
It was there . I know it was , because I saw it only yesterday .

565
01:04:24,760 --> 01:04:27,366
I really don 't understand who could have moved it .

566
01:04:34,800 --> 01:04:37,690
The driver of the hearse might 've lied to the Frontier Official

567
01:04:37,760 --> 01:04:39,250
about where he was going .

568
01:04:39,320 --> 01:04:41,527
Yes , but that fellow at the morgue wasn 't lying .

569
01:04:41,600 --> 01:04:43,576
He was really surprised when he saw the coffin wasn 't there .

570
01:04:43,600 --> 01:04:45,728
He must have had it sometime .

571
01:04:45,800 --> 01:04:50,681
- I think he 's still somewhere here in Karlstadt . - But where ? This is a big town .

572
01:04:51,280 --> 01:04:53,176
There are not many places he can hide , don 't forget .

573
01:04:53,200 --> 01:04:54,281
There is that , of course .

574
01:04:55,560 --> 01:04:57,961
What are you two being so mysterious about over there ?

575
01:04:58,720 --> 01:05:01,564
We 'll be with you in a moment , my darling .

576
01:05:03,440 --> 01:05:07,411
There is an old neglected graveyard about three miles from here .

577
01:05:08,040 --> 01:05:10,042
Somewhere in this area .

578
01:05:11,080 --> 01:05:12,525
St Joseph 's .

579
01:05:14,560 --> 01:05:16,164
Just one moment .

580
01:05:20,120 --> 01:05:23,044
Mina , my dear , don 't think I 'm being silly ,

581
01:05:23,560 --> 01:05:26,803
but I 'd feel much happier , if during my absence , you would wear this for me .

582
01:05:27,880 --> 01:05:31,327
Please don 't ask me why , but just wear it for my sake .

583
01:05:33,720 --> 01:05:37,008
- Arthur , I ... - Please , Mina .

584
01:05:41,080 --> 01:05:42,525
( GASPING )

585
01:05:45,320 --> 01:05:47,561
( DRAMATIC INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

586
01:06:16,720 --> 01:06:20,122
You said Lucy would lead us to Dracula . Why didn 't I listen to you ?

587
01:06:20,200 --> 01:06:21,770
This would never have happened .

588
01:06:21,840 --> 01:06:23,216
You mustn 't blame yourself for that ,

589
01:06:23,240 --> 01:06:26,289
but you must have the courage to let Mina lead us now .

590
01:06:26,360 --> 01:06:28,647
We 'll give her every protection we can .

591
01:06:28,720 --> 01:06:30,176
Tonight we 'll watch the windows of her room .

592
01:06:30,200 --> 01:06:33,568
- They face two sides of the house , don 't they ? - Yes .

593
01:06:36,720 --> 01:06:40,520
I know I ask a great deal of you , but you mustn 't weaken now .

594
01:06:40,600 --> 01:06:44,207
We have it within our power to rid the world of this evil .

595
01:06:47,520 --> 01:06:50,251
And , with God 's help , we 'll succeed .

596
01:07:14,520 --> 01:07:16,010
( WOLF HOWLING )

597
01:08:15,520 --> 01:08:18,524
( SINISTER INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

598
01:09:18,400 --> 01:09:19,731
( SUDDEN SCREECHING )

599
01:09:46,800 --> 01:09:49,976
Mina 's safe now , but we must keep watch again tonight . You 'd better get some rest .

600
01:09:50,000 --> 01:09:52,810
- What about you ? - I 'll be all right in there , if I may .

601
01:09:52,880 --> 01:09:54,041
Right .

602
01:09:54,360 --> 01:09:56,806
- I 'll get you a rug from our room . - Thank you .

603
01:10:05,120 --> 01:10:06,610
ARTHUR : Mina !

604
01:10:06,680 --> 01:10:08,808
( FRANTIC INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

605
01:11:25,600 --> 01:11:27,648
Just sit still like that for a minute .

606
01:11:45,000 --> 01:11:46,331
Thank you .

607
01:11:56,560 --> 01:11:59,040
- Will she be all right ? - I think so .

608
01:12:06,840 --> 01:12:08,649
Let me see your arm .

609
01:12:09,320 --> 01:12:10,560
Steady .

610
01:12:12,000 --> 01:12:13,684
Are you all right ?

611
01:12:17,760 --> 01:12:19,762
Yes . Yes , it 's very good .

612
01:12:24,680 --> 01:12:28,651
Now , you 'll need plenty of fluid . Tea , coffee or , better still , wine .

613
01:12:28,720 --> 01:12:31,644
Go down and have some now , there 's a good fellow .

614
01:12:43,960 --> 01:12:47,043
Don 't worry , Gerda and I will take care of her .

615
01:13:00,560 --> 01:13:03,216
Just bathe her forehead , will you , Gerda ? With eau de cologne or something .

616
01:13:03,240 --> 01:13:04,526
Yes , sir .

617
01:13:21,960 --> 01:13:24,804
- How is she now ? - She 's reacted very well .

618
01:13:25,400 --> 01:13:26,400
Thank God !

619
01:13:28,800 --> 01:13:32,009
How did he get in ? We watched the house all night .

620
01:13:32,320 --> 01:13:35,164
Your theory must be wrong . He can change into something else .

621
01:13:35,240 --> 01:13:38,449
He must be able to . How else could he have got in ?

622
01:13:40,040 --> 01:13:41,565
I wish I knew .

623
01:13:44,400 --> 01:13:47,244
- Madam is sleeping now , sir . - She mustn 't be left .

624
01:13:47,320 --> 01:13:49,641
I 'll go up to her . I 'd like to .

625
01:13:50,240 --> 01:13:54,245
You stay and rest , and have some wine . I 'm sure you need both .

626
01:13:54,320 --> 01:13:58,530
- Gerda , will you fetch another bottle ? - Oh , sir , I don 't like to .

627
01:13:59,320 --> 01:14:02,369
You know what happened last time when I disobeyed Mrs Holmwood 's orders .

628
01:14:02,440 --> 01:14:03,646
What do you mean ?

629
01:14:03,720 --> 01:14:07,441
Well , sir , Madam told me the other day that I must , on no account , go down to the cellar .

630
01:14:10,120 --> 01:14:11,565
( FAST-PACED INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

631
01:14:20,280 --> 01:14:21,361
( HISSES )

632
01:14:32,840 --> 01:14:36,128
Holmwood ! Holmwood !

633
01:14:38,120 --> 01:14:39,360
Holmwood !

634
01:14:47,240 --> 01:14:48,890
( GERDA SCREAMING )

635
01:14:51,840 --> 01:14:53,410
( GERDA WAILING )

636
01:14:54,600 --> 01:14:56,682
Gerda , what happened ?

637
01:14:58,920 --> 01:15:01,924
You said I was to come back to Madam , so I came up here .

638
01:15:02,000 --> 01:15:05,288
- And he looked like the devil ! - Gerda ! Now , what happened ?

639
01:15:06,520 --> 01:15:10,206
He came in here and he picked Madam up like she was a baby !

640
01:15:10,720 --> 01:15:12,768
Calm yourself , Gerda . Calm yourself .

641
01:15:13,200 --> 01:15:16,602
There 's only one place he can make for now . His home .

642
01:15:32,840 --> 01:15:36,287
It 's a coach driver . He 's been dead about half an hour .

643
01:15:47,880 --> 01:15:49,689
You think Dracula killed that coachman ?

644
01:15:49,760 --> 01:15:52,889
Of course he did . Without a coach he 'd never get home before sunrise .

645
01:15:52,960 --> 01:15:53,961
He 'd be dead .

646
01:15:54,040 --> 01:15:56,896
- But even if he does get home ... - He 'd hide in the castle vaults for years .

647
01:15:56,920 --> 01:15:59,571
- We 'd lose him there . - And Mina ?

648
01:16:10,920 --> 01:16:11,967
( HORSES NEIGHING )

649
01:16:12,200 --> 01:16:13,964
- ( CRASHING ) - ( GASPS )

650
01:16:24,800 --> 01:16:25,847
Oh !

651
01:16:28,080 --> 01:16:29,684
Hey ! ( COUGHING )

652
01:16:45,440 --> 01:16:48,046
Halt !

653
01:16:48,120 --> 01:16:49,531
( LOUD CRASH )

654
01:16:59,640 --> 01:17:01,324
It 's getting light .

655
01:17:03,960 --> 01:17:06,122
( DRAMATIC INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

656
01:17:23,240 --> 01:17:24,765
( SCREAMS )

657
01:17:33,080 --> 01:17:34,081
ARTHUR : Whoa !

658
01:17:35,320 --> 01:17:36,446
Look !

659
01:17:38,960 --> 01:17:41,247
( FAST-PACED INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

660
01:18:26,560 --> 01:18:28,085
( BOTH GRUNTING )

661
01:19:13,120 --> 01:19:14,281
( SCREAMING )

662
01:19:19,360 --> 01:19:20,600
( GASPING )

663
01:19:38,520 --> 01:19:39,646
( MOANING )

664
01:20:12,960 --> 01:20:14,962
( SOFT INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

665
01:20:56,840 --> 01:20:58,968
( SOLEMN INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC )

